Run:

```bash
curl -sS -D - -o /dev/null https://geoguessing.me/auth/google
```

You should receive a `302` redirect to a Google Accounts URL.

Then open this in your browser:

```text
https://geoguessing.me/auth/google
```

Complete the Google login. Google should redirect back to:

```text
https://geoguessing.me/auth/google/callback
```

The application should then redirect to:

```text
https://geoguessing.me
```

## Common errors

### `redirect_uri_mismatch`

Make sure both places contain exactly:

```text
https://geoguessing.me/auth/google/callback
```

It must match:

```dotenv
GOOGLE_CALLBACK_URL=https://geoguessing.me/auth/google/callback
```

and the Google Cloud **Authorized redirect URI**.

### `Google OAuth is not configured`

One or more of these variables is missing inside the container:

```dotenv
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET
GOOGLE_CALLBACK_URL
```

Recreate the container with `--force-recreate`.

### `invalid_client`

The client ID or secret is wrong. If your teammate created the original client and cannot provide the secret, create a new client secret or create a new web client. Google supports rotating client secrets without changing the application code. [Google client-secret rotation](https://support.google.com/cloud/answer/15549257)

### `Access blocked: This app’s request is invalid`

Usually one of these is wrong:

- The account is not listed as a test user.
- The app is configured for the wrong audience.
- The redirect URI is incorrect.
- The OAuth client belongs to a different Google Cloud project than the configured credentials.

### Login succeeds but the session does not persist

Confirm that production contains:

```dotenv
NODE_ENV=production
FRONTEND_URL=https://geoguessing.me
```

Your code marks the authentication cookie as secure in production, so the site must be accessed through HTTPS.

