The Caddy image downloaded correctly. The error is only because `validate` must be run through the `caddy` executable.

Run this corrected command:

```bash
docker compose \
  --env-file .env.production \
  -f docker-compose.production.yml \
  run --rm --no-deps \
  --entrypoint caddy \
  caddy \
  validate \
  --config /etc/caddy/Caddyfile \
  --adapter caddyfile
```

You should see:

```text
Valid configuration
```

The volumes and Docker network created during validation are normal and can remain.

If validation succeeds, start the deployment:

```bash
docker compose \
  --env-file .env.production \
  -f docker-compose.production.yml \
  up -d
```

Then check the status:

```bash
docker compose \
  --env-file .env.production \
  -f docker-compose.production.yml \
  ps
```

If validation instead reports that `/etc/caddy/Caddyfile` cannot be found, verify that your VM has:

```bash
ls -l caddy/Caddyfile
```

and that the Compose file contains:

```yaml
volumes:
  - ./caddy:/etc/caddy:ro
```
